00:16:14.073 --> 00:16:15.274
It's ridiculous.

00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:16.742
I'm going to reverse that.

00:16:16.742 --> 00:16:21.080 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Do you think that Gavin
Newsom thinks he's doing well?

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.948
- Well, how many interviews
have you seen Gavin Newsom

00:16:22.948 --> 00:16:24.183
have in the last several months?

00:16:24.183 --> 00:16:24.984
- We've reached out
a million dollars.

00:16:24.984 --> 00:16:26.218
- Of course not.

00:16:26.218 --> 00:16:27.453 align:start size:84% position:16%
How's he going to
defend rising crime?

00:16:27.453 --> 00:16:28.821 align:start size:88% position:13%
How's he going to defend
these crappy schools

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:30.923
he wouldn't put his
own kids in on a bet?

00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:34.960
How's he going to defend
basically buying a home

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.729
for homeless at 10
times or five times

00:16:36.729 --> 00:16:38.731
the cost of what the
private sector can do?

00:16:38.731 --> 00:16:40.933
How's he going to defend
any of that? He cannot.

00:16:40.933 --> 00:16:43.102
How's he going to defend
how ticked off people are

00:16:43.102 --> 00:16:45.371
about the arrogant way
he shut down the state

00:16:45.371 --> 00:16:46.605
in the most severe way

00:16:46.605 --> 00:16:48.507
than any of the other
50 governors have done?

00:16:48.507 --> 00:16:50.809
He can't defend that,
he doesn't want you.

00:16:52.011 --> 00:16:54.113
In the 33 years that
Buckley had his show

00:16:54.113 --> 00:16:55.848
called, "Firing Line".

00:16:55.848 --> 00:16:57.816
The last day he ended
the show somebody said,

00:16:57.816 --> 00:17:00.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
why didn't Ted Robert
Kennedy and all the times

00:17:00.152 --> 00:17:02.321 align:start size:97% position:3%
you extended him an
invitation, come on your show?

00:17:02.321 --> 00:17:04.957 align:start size:97% position:3%
And Buckley said, why does
the baloney avoid the grinder?

00:17:04.957 --> 00:17:06.558
He doesn't want you,
he doesn't want me.

00:17:06.558 --> 00:17:07.493
He can't defend that.

00:17:07.493 --> 00:17:08.494
He's not going to debate me.

00:17:08.494 --> 00:17:10.029
Are you kidding,
are you kidding?

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:11.463
- So what do you need to happen?

00:17:11.463 --> 00:17:14.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think, you're
on the ballot, like,

00:17:14.133 --> 00:17:15.434
what do you think has to happen

00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:16.368 align:start size:97% position:3%
over the course of the next--
- I need money.

00:17:16.368 --> 00:17:17.302
- It's not a ton of time.

00:17:17.302 --> 00:17:18.237
- I, I need, I need money.

00:17:18.237 --> 00:17:20.406
When I was induced to run

00:17:20.406 --> 00:17:21.907
by people that I
like and respect--

00:17:21.907 --> 00:17:24.376
- By the way speaking, you
mentioned Prager before,

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.345
I said to Prager in my
backyard months ago,

00:17:26.345 --> 00:17:28.680 align:start size:88% position:13%
I said, Dennis run,
I'll fundraise for you.

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.282 align:start size:84% position:16%
You could have parties
here, whatever.

00:17:30.282 --> 00:17:31.917
Everything I can
do on my channel.

00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:33.986 align:start size:97% position:3%
- What'd he say?
- He goes, get Larry Elder.

00:17:33.986 --> 00:17:37.189
- Get Larry Elder to do it,
get the black guy to do it.

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:39.792 align:start size:97% position:3%
And Dennis is also responsible
for my career on radio.

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:41.026 align:start size:84% position:16%
But for Dennis, I
met him in Cleveland

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:42.294
when I was working.

00:17:42.294 --> 00:17:43.529
I'm from here, but I
met him in Cleveland

00:17:43.529 --> 00:17:45.397
and Dennis put me on his show.

00:17:45.397 --> 00:17:47.199
Management heard me
the rest is history.

00:17:47.199 --> 00:17:49.101
And Dennis also induced
me to get into this race.

00:17:49.101 --> 00:17:50.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told Dennis this
morning I was on his show.

00:17:50.702 --> 00:17:52.871
I said, "Dennis, you're
going to burn in hell."

00:17:53.872 --> 00:17:54.807
What are we talking about?

00:17:54.807 --> 00:17:55.741
- We're all going together.

00:17:55.741 --> 00:17:57.176
- I lost my train of thought.

00:17:57.176 --> 00:17:58.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
- No, so in the two months
now it's it's money.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.378
Okay, so you got it your mind.

00:17:59.378 --> 00:18:01.313
- Okay, so I was told
by people like Dennis

00:18:01.313 --> 00:18:02.981 align:start size:84% position:16%
and people like pastor
Jackie and others,

00:18:02.981 --> 00:18:04.683
Larry, because of
your celebrity,

00:18:04.683 --> 00:18:07.653
because of your social
media profile platform,

00:18:07.653 --> 00:18:09.688
you got 2.5 million, I think
you have a little bit more.

00:18:09.688 --> 00:18:12.424
- Yeah, they're screwing
you on Twitter, by the way.

00:18:12.424 --> 00:18:14.827
You're like right
up there on that,

00:18:14.827 --> 00:18:17.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Have a channel called Larry
Elder Epic Times Channel.

00:18:17.996 --> 00:18:20.699
I have 575,000 followers.

00:18:20.699 --> 00:18:23.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had that same
number for almost a year.

00:18:23.268 --> 00:18:24.536
It was rocking and rolling

00:18:24.536 --> 00:18:25.938
and then all of a
sudden, dead stop.

00:18:25.938 --> 00:18:27.439 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, no, I know, because
me and you were both

00:18:27.439 --> 00:18:30.075
at like 980 on Twitter and I
was like, I want to beat him.

00:18:30.075 --> 00:18:30.909 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Not that we're competitive
or anything like that.

00:18:30.909 --> 00:18:31.977
- No, no, no!

00:18:33.178 --> 00:18:34.646
You know, you beat
me once publicly.

00:18:34.646 --> 00:18:35.848 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I was like, I got to
get to a million before him

00:18:35.848 --> 00:18:37.282 align:start size:81% position:19%
and then they just
keep, get you.

00:18:38.417 --> 00:18:40.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So the whole thing
is about money.

00:18:40.018 --> 00:18:42.087 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's why I'm urging people
to go to electelder.com.

00:18:42.087 --> 00:18:43.622
Notice how I didn't work
that in until just now?

00:18:43.622 --> 00:18:45.691 align:start size:84% position:16%
- No, no it's subtle.
- I waited on it.

00:18:45.691 --> 00:18:46.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
I started to do it
right away but I said,

00:18:46.525 --> 00:18:47.826
you know, Dave, well.

00:18:47.826 --> 00:18:50.529
- That was electelder--
- Electelder.com, yes.

00:18:51.964 --> 00:18:54.032
And so I was told, unlike
the average politician,

00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:55.934
you're not going to be on
the phone 75% of the time

00:18:55.934 --> 00:18:57.603
raising money because
you're so well known

00:18:57.603 --> 00:18:59.438
and all I have to do is tell
people that you're going to run

00:18:59.438 --> 00:19:01.073 align:start position:0%
and all of a sudden the
money's gonna come flooding in.

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:03.242
I'm on the phone with 75% of
the time trying to raise money,

00:19:03.242 --> 00:19:05.144
just like any other politician.

00:19:05.144 --> 00:19:09.681
There's a $34,200 limit max
individual contribution,

00:19:09.681 --> 00:19:11.416 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm sure you're going
to be making that, Dave.

00:19:11.416 --> 00:19:14.453
- Well, I'll have to
talk my accountant.

00:19:14.453 --> 00:19:16.021 align:start size:84% position:16%
My accountant's
over here, you know.

00:19:16.021 --> 00:19:18.190
- But Gavin Newsom does not
have spending limitations

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.458
nor raising limitations.

00:19:19.458 --> 00:19:22.361
He can spin and raise as
much money as possible.

00:19:22.361 --> 00:19:23.362
Shortly after it was obvious--

00:19:23.362 --> 00:19:24.563
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:19:24.563 --> 00:19:26.798 align:start size:88% position:13%
So the incumbent can
raise whatever they want

00:19:26.798 --> 00:19:28.066
from whoever they want?

00:19:28.066 --> 00:19:30.068
- But yeah, by the way,
the five-year tax stuff

00:19:30.068 --> 00:19:33.205 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I had to return, that
that is apparently the problem

00:19:33.205 --> 00:19:35.707
by my getting on
the ballot, again,

00:19:35.707 --> 00:19:37.442
that's going to be
overturned, I'm sure,

00:19:37.442 --> 00:19:38.944
does not apply to him.

00:19:38.944 --> 00:19:41.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
He does not have to turn
over five years of his taxes.

00:19:42.781 --> 00:19:44.249
Just the rivals.

00:19:44.249 --> 00:19:45.717
- I'll put that one aside,
but why doesn't the incumbent

00:19:45.717 --> 00:19:47.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
have any limitations
on what he can-

00:19:47.152 --> 00:19:49.321
- You tell me. It's California.

00:19:49.321 --> 00:19:50.722
- What a town, man.

00:19:50.722 --> 00:19:52.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
We are in La-La Land.
- Chinatown Jake.

00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:56.295 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I do, I have limitations
on more than that.

00:19:56.295 --> 00:19:59.665 align:start position:0%
I cannot win unless I get
money from people in California

00:19:59.665 --> 00:20:02.501 align:start size:97% position:3%
and outside California, who
recognize how California goes.

00:20:02.501 --> 00:20:04.069
So goes the rest of the country.

00:20:04.069 --> 00:20:05.671 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And I want "millionaires
and billionaires",

00:20:05.671 --> 00:20:09.241 line:0%
to quote Bernie Sanders,
set up PACS along the lines

00:20:09.241 --> 00:20:11.143 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
of my philosophy
about school choice,

00:20:11.143 --> 00:20:12.110
about what to do about crime,

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.312
what to do about homelessness

00:20:13.312 --> 00:20:15.214
so that I can spend beyond that.

00:20:15.214 --> 00:20:17.115
Otherwise, I'm not going to win.

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:19.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
Shortly after it was
obvious I was going to run,

00:20:19.084 --> 00:20:21.420
a union gave this
man $5 million.

00:20:23.021 --> 00:20:25.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
So without getting
money from other people

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.259 align:start position:0%
and outside other people to
set up little action committee,

00:20:27.259 --> 00:20:28.994 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's along the lines
of my philosophy,

00:20:28.994 --> 00:20:30.562
I don't have any hope
of beating this guy.

00:20:30.562 --> 00:20:32.931
- So you consider yourself a
small L libertarian, right?

00:20:32.931 --> 00:20:34.533
- Yes, yes.

00:20:34.533 --> 00:20:36.868 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've always been that and
I'm a registered Republican.

00:20:36.868 --> 00:20:39.271 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the reason I registered
as Republican, about,

00:20:39.271 --> 00:20:40.572
I think it was 12 years ago,

00:20:40.572 --> 00:20:42.007
is I was going to run
against Barbara Boxer.

00:20:42.007 --> 00:20:42.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't gonna run
against as a libertarian.

00:20:42.841 --> 00:20:44.376
They always lose.

00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:47.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
And by the way, this is
kind of one of the reasons

00:20:47.045 --> 00:20:48.880
I want to go into politics,

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
I had such such a
bad experience then.

00:20:50.449 --> 00:20:52.951
Ten they said, go
to Washington, DC,

00:20:52.951 --> 00:20:55.621
meet the Senate people, John
Cornyn, who's still there,

00:20:55.621 --> 00:20:58.090 align:start size:88% position:13%
and Inhofe from
Oklahoma is still there,

00:20:58.090 --> 00:20:59.758
and just show them
how charming you are,

00:20:59.758 --> 00:21:01.293
give them your backstory
and then they'll back you

00:21:01.293 --> 00:21:04.596
as the official candidate
and the money will come in.

00:21:04.596 --> 00:21:06.498
I fly to DC on my own dime.

00:21:06.498 --> 00:21:09.501
I didn't want there
to be any shenanigans

00:21:09.501 --> 00:21:11.103 align:start size:81% position:19%
and I sit there
with, with Cornyn.

00:21:11.103 --> 00:21:13.372 align:start position:0%
I tell them about my background
and talk about my father

00:21:13.372 --> 00:21:15.207
and how he came to
California in 1945,

00:21:15.207 --> 00:21:17.142
he was a Marine and all this.

00:21:17.142 --> 00:21:18.543
And they're, (mouth noises).

00:21:19.411 --> 00:21:20.512
I thought I'd won them over.

00:21:20.512 --> 00:21:21.780
I get back to LAX, phone rings,

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.582
we're going with Carly Fiorina.

00:21:23.582 --> 00:21:25.384
I said, why, they
said three reasons.

00:21:25.384 --> 00:21:26.618
One, she's a woman.

00:21:26.618 --> 00:21:28.453 align:start size:88% position:13%
I said, well, I'm not
gonna have a sex to run.

00:21:28.453 --> 00:21:29.588
Number two, she has
more money than you.

00:21:29.588 --> 00:21:31.089
I said, I give you that.

00:21:31.089 --> 00:21:32.824
Number three, she has higher
name recognition than you do.

00:21:32.824 --> 00:21:34.326
I said, no, she doesn't.

00:21:34.326 --> 00:21:36.528
She does in DC because she
was CEO of Hewlett Packard.

00:21:36.528 --> 00:21:38.030
But nobody knows her
out here in California.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:40.332 align:start position:0%
She lost by 10 points and
didn't put nearly as much money

00:21:40.332 --> 00:21:42.434
into her campaign
as they thought.

00:21:42.434 --> 00:21:44.870
So that was my only
foray into politics.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.505
Other than when I ran
against William Maury

00:21:46.505 --> 00:21:47.673
for fifth grade class president.

00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:48.640
- How'd you do?

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:49.808
- I took three out of four rows,

00:21:49.808 --> 00:21:51.643 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're still
cleaning up the blood.

00:21:51.643 --> 00:21:54.780 align:start position:0%
So I just was turned off by
the whole thing about politics.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:55.814
- Yeah, well, I know you--

00:21:55.814 --> 00:21:57.649
- And how duplicitous it is.

00:21:57.649 --> 00:22:00.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
And many people I thought were
gonna give me money didn't

00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.754
and those who didn't think
was gonna give me money did.

00:22:02.754 --> 00:22:05.390
And I'm still surprised
all the time by the games

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:08.327
that people play and the
shenanigans people play.

00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:11.730
But I am now old enough

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.633
and I think wise enough and
experienced enough in life

00:22:14.633 --> 00:22:16.735 align:start size:88% position:13%
to understand these
things are gonna happen.

00:22:16.735 --> 00:22:18.236
I was asked many times,

00:22:18.236 --> 00:22:20.072
what is your experience
for running for governor?

00:22:20.072 --> 00:22:21.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, what does
Gavin Newsom's experience?

00:22:21.873 --> 00:22:24.776
- He was mayor of San Francisco.

00:22:24.776 --> 00:22:27.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was eight years--
- Eight years, ruined it!

00:22:27.045 --> 00:22:28.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Eight years,
Lieutenant Governor,

00:22:28.213 --> 00:22:30.015
two years of current governor.

00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:31.516
How's he doing?

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:34.019 align:start size:97% position:3%
There was a fellow who ran for
governor, served two terms,

00:22:34.019 --> 00:22:35.487
ran for president
served two terms.

00:22:35.487 --> 00:22:37.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
His name is Ronald Reagan
came out of the movie industry

00:22:37.155 --> 00:22:38.390
for crying out loud.

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:39.591
I've got common sense,
I got good judgment,

00:22:39.591 --> 00:22:40.792
I'm a native California,

00:22:40.792 --> 00:22:42.027
I'm a product of public schools,

00:22:42.027 --> 00:22:43.328
I know what's wrong with them.

00:22:43.328 --> 00:22:45.130
I have got ideas what to
do about homelessness.

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:47.199 align:start size:81% position:19%
I know what we
can do about crime

00:22:47.199 --> 00:22:48.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know we can do
about the cost of living.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:50.869
So when I become governor,

00:22:50.869 --> 00:22:53.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to use my powers
to declare emergencies

00:22:53.271 --> 00:22:54.573
for many of these issues.

00:22:54.573 --> 00:22:56.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have the same
water infrastructure

00:22:56.375 --> 00:22:58.410 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the same power
infrastructure as we had

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:00.679
when California was
half the population.

00:23:00.679 --> 00:23:02.547
Because if you stick
a spoon in the ground,

00:23:02.547 --> 00:23:03.849
someone's going to
sue you claiming

00:23:03.849 --> 00:23:06.218 align:start position:0%
has had an adverse
environmental impact under CEQA.

00:23:06.218 --> 00:23:08.153
I'm going to stop all that crap.

00:23:08.153 --> 00:23:10.722
- So, when Newsom's
doing all of this,

00:23:10.722 --> 00:23:12.824 align:start size:97% position:3%
like the average person,
especially during lockdowns,

00:23:12.824 --> 00:23:15.060
I would go to a lot of the
rallies to open up the state

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:16.561
and I was meeting, you know,

00:23:16.561 --> 00:23:19.131 align:start size:97% position:3%
people that own restaurants
and people that own businesses

00:23:19.131 --> 00:23:20.499
that they were not political,

00:23:20.499 --> 00:23:22.200
they certainly were
not Republicans,

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:24.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
but they were mugged
basically, mugged by reality.

00:23:24.569 --> 00:23:26.471
And they were going, I
just want to go to work.

00:23:26.471 --> 00:23:29.007
I have a feeling a lot
of them can be broken

00:23:29.007 --> 00:23:31.109 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they can move to say
the conservative side

00:23:31.109 --> 00:23:32.811
or Republican or
Larry Elder thing.

00:23:32.811 --> 00:23:34.212
But what do you think is,

00:23:34.212 --> 00:23:35.414 align:start size:97% position:3%
do you think there's
something else you got to do

00:23:35.414 --> 00:23:37.416
to get them to make
that final jump?

00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:38.483
- Well, that's why
I need the money.

00:23:38.483 --> 00:23:39.684
I need to be on television.

00:23:39.684 --> 00:23:41.253 align:start size:84% position:16%
California is a
big, big, big state,

00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:43.422 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you need to be on TV
and you need to be on radio.

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:47.058
But Dave, it doesn't take
long find horror stories.

00:23:47.058 --> 00:23:48.460
I mean, literally they
just come up to you.

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:50.228 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't even have
to go look for them.

00:23:50.228 --> 00:23:53.498
The other day I'm shooting
a commercial for my ads,

00:23:53.498 --> 00:23:54.633
for running for office.

00:23:55.767 --> 00:23:57.269 align:start size:84% position:16%
Makeup lady's
putting stuff on me.

00:23:57.269 --> 00:23:58.470
